Kind: widen
Issue: #954
Holds open: spins for 50 ms, or until the wakee has run, between the look at handoff_wakee and the waker's leaving for the high thread, so that a tick may let the wakee take the waker's processor before it leaves, every time
Run: --entry 67 300 -smp 4

diff --git a/uros/src/mach_kernel/x86_64/cpu/wakee_test.c b/uros/src/mach_kernel/x86_64/cpu/wakee_test.c
index 5d13982f..9220d00e 100644
--- a/uros/src/mach_kernel/x86_64/cpu/wakee_test.c
+++ b/uros/src/mach_kernel/x86_64/cpu/wakee_test.c
@@ -202,6 +202,14 @@ wakee_test(void)
 	self->handoff_target = THREAD_NULL;
 	self->handoff_hint = FALSE;
 	mp_enable_preemption();
+	/* 954-widen-before-leaving: 50 ms of ticks before this thread leaves,
+	 * at which the wakee may take this processor first */
+	{
+		uint64_t	w0 = rdtsc();
+
+		while (!wakee_test_wakee_ran && rdtsc() - w0 < hz / 20)
+			cpu_pause();
+	}
 
 	/* And this thread leaves, with something better than the wakee here. */
 	thread_wakeup((event_t) &wakee_test_high_event);
